      ],
      "source": "https://wipi.ai.kr/en/Kalaoa,%20Hawaii",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Kalaoa sits on the lower western slopes of Hualalai and stretches to the Pacific Ocean.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalaoa%2C_Hawaii",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 19th and early‑20th centuries, sugarcane and Kona coffee plantations, like Pahala, shaped the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wipi.ai.kr/en/Kalaoa,%20Hawaii",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After World War II, land subdivision turned much of the former plantations into the residential community we see today.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://wipi.ai.kr/en/Kalaoa,%20Hawaii",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Keahole Point hosts the Natural Energy Laboratory of Hawaii, part of the Kaloko‑Honokohau National Historical Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
